<title>GREECE: GREEK CPI INFLATION STEADY AT 8.5PCT Y/Y IN SEPT.</title>
<headline>GREEK CPI INFLATION STEADY AT 8.5PCT Y/Y IN SEPT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greek consumer price inflation was</p>
<p>unchanged at 8.5 percent year-on-year in September, the National</p>
<p>Statistics Service (NSS) said.</p>
<p>September food prices rose by 1.9 percent month-on-month,</p>
<p>apparel and footwear by 7.8 percent, education-entertainment by</p>
<p>6.3 percent, durable consumer goods by 6.1 percent and housing</p>
<p>by 1.5 percent, it said.</p>
<p>Greek bankers and economists polled by Reuters had predicted</p>
<p>that inflation would be steady at 8.5 percent.</p>
<p>    Consumer Price Index   September 96 August 96  September 95</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		 3.0	   0.0%	  3.0%</p>
<p>    Rate of change		 8.5%	  8.5%	  8.4%</p>
<p>    Index (1988=100)	   290.1	 281.7	 267.4</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
